Subject: [PATCH] luci: use kernel CPUFreq and show W1701K diagnostic state accurately

Remove direct-PLL override controls, RPC and /dev/mem ACL so userspace
cannot bypass PM-domain serialization. Use neutral Ethernet DMA labels,
report NPU driver binding separately from active offload, and hide invalid
translated tuples/MAC fields until PPE entries are bound.

--- a/package/luci-app-airoha-npu/root/usr/libexec/rpcd/luci.airoha_npu
+++ b/package/luci-app-airoha-npu/root/usr/libexec/rpcd/luci.airoha_npu
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
-# Airoha SoC Status RPC backend for LuCI (NPU + CPU + Overclock)
+# Airoha SoC Status RPC backend for LuCI (NPU + CPUFreq)
 
 . /lib/functions.sh
 
